Subject: [PATCH] No grid to see in the dust, and clumps

Patch 0043 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-08: "the particles are too uniform almost, like they don't have enough
dispersity, and they feel like they're just along the lines of invisible cubes".

Three things drew the cubes. The cells lay along the world's axes, the lines of every wall and
floor; each mote was kept in the middle 80% of its cell, which left an empty slab on every face;
and the march sampled the ray every half cell, so it could cross a cell's corner without looking in
it. The cells are now turned by a fixed rotation (DustLattice) that lines up with nothing, the march
walks every cell the ray crosses in order (a 3D DDA, at most DustMaxCells), and a mote may sit
anywhere in its cell, its wander held to 90% of the way to the nearest face so it never leaves the
cell it is looked for in.

The density is no longer even: a smooth noise over cells DustClumpCells across scales it from
nothing to twice the row's, about the row's on average, so the dust gathers in drifts with clear
air between.

diff --git a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
--- a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
+++ b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
@@ -1609,7 +1609,6 @@ float3 windOffset(float seconds) {
 // motes in front of a near wall faded out). A long reach takes longer steps, at most 128 of them
 // to a ray; the far motes it then misses are the ones the fade has all but taken already.
 static const float AmbienceFadeStart = 0.2f;  // the share of the distance where the fade begins
-static const uint DustMaxSteps = 128;
 static const uint DustMaxMovers = 4;          // the movers near one ray that push the motes it passes
 static const float AirPushLimit = 100.0f;     // patch 0039: world units at most that the movers together push a mote
 
@@ -1624,12 +1623,48 @@ float3 airPush(float3 x, uint movers[DustMaxMovers], uint moverCount) {
     return (pushedLength > AirPushLimit) ? (pushed * (AirPushLimit / pushedLength)) : pushed;
 }
 
+// NO GRID TO SEE, AND CLUMPS (patch 0043, the user, 2026-10-08: "the particles are too uniform
+// almost, like they don't have enough dispersity, and they feel like they're just along the lines
+// of invisible cubes"). Three things made the cubes: the cells lay along the world's own axes, the
+// same lines as the walls and the floor; each mote was kept off its cell's faces (the middle 80%),
+// leaving an empty slab on every face; and the march sampled the ray every half cell, so it could
+// cut across a cell's corner without looking in it. Now the cells are turned (DustLattice, a fixed
+// rotation that lines up with nothing the game builds), the march visits every cell the ray
+// crosses, in order (a 3D DDA), and a mote may sit anywhere in its cell: its wander shrinks near a
+// face, so it never leaves the cell it is looked for in.
+//
+// And the dust is not one even density: a slow noise over cells several wide thins it to almost
+// nothing in places and thickens it in others, about the same on average, so it gathers in drifts
+// and leaves clear air between.
+static const float3x3 DustLattice = {
+    0.691148f, -0.573403f, 0.439913f,
+    0.648256f, 0.760957f, -0.026610f,
+    -0.319497f, 0.303568f, 0.897646f
+};
+static const float DustClumpCells = 3.5f;     // cells across one clump or gap
+static const uint DustMaxCells = 192;         // cells one ray visits at most; the far ones are faded out
+
+// How thick the dust is in this cell, as a share of the row's: 0 to 2, about 1 on average.
+float dustClump(int3 cell) {
+    const float3 q = float3(cell) / DustClumpCells;
+    const float3 i = floor(q);
+    const float3 f = q - i;
+    const float3 u = f * f * (3.0f - 2.0f * f);
+    float n = 0.0f;
+    for (uint c = 0; c < 8u; c++) {
+        const int3 corner = int3(i) + int3(int(c & 1u), int((c >> 1) & 1u), int((c >> 2) & 1u));
+        const float value = float(dustHash(uint4(uint3(corner), 0x5BD1E995u)).x) * (1.0f / 4294967295.0f);
+        const float3 w = float3(((c & 1u) != 0u) ? u.x : (1.0f - u.x), ((c & 2u) != 0u) ? u.y : (1.0f - u.y), ((c & 4u) != 0u) ? u.z : (1.0f - u.z));
+        n += value * w.x * w.y * w.z;
+    }
+
+    return 2.0f * smoothstep(0.2f, 0.8f, n);
+}
